   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
-    "title": "Confirm cost, inheritance and shared parent invoices",
-    "body": "<p>Open <b>Vendor &amp; Payments</b> on a detail line to choose its vendor and agreed base/fringe amounts. Confirm cost preserves the original budget and records the decision. Blank confirmed fields follow current budget values; explicit amounts remain separate from the estimate.</p><p>Account/sub-account six-dot menus or currency signs open parent pages. Set a default Vendor / crew member and Paid through; children inherit unless overridden. Direct payment (override parent) clears inherited payroll handling. Changing defaults does not rewrite historical payment recipients.</p><p>A parent invoice is stored once. Apply it to included detail lines and review proportional, equal or manual base/fringe allocations. Exact shares must sum to the invoice total. Child pages show their shares, not repeated whole-invoice costs. Keep different suppliers on separate detail lines.</p>"
+    "title": "Details, expected cost and shared parent invoices",
+    "body": "<p>Open <b>Vendor &amp; Payments</b> on a detail line to open Details. Choose Vendor / crew / cast when known and Paid through if needed; the + creates a contact without losing the draft. Enter Expected base and confirm it with Confirm Expected. Fringes follow the line’s budget settings. Blank follows the budget. Confirmation preserves Budgeted and does not post a payment. A prior manually entered fringe override is replaced only when you confirm.</p><p>Account/sub-account six-dot menus or currency signs open parent pages. Set a default Vendor / crew member and Paid through; children inherit unless overridden. Direct payment (override parent) clears inherited payroll handling. Changing defaults does not rewrite historical payment recipients.</p><p>A parent invoice is stored once. Apply it to included detail lines and review proportional, equal or manual base/fringe allocations. Exact shares must sum to the invoice total. Child pages show their shares, not repeated whole-invoice costs. Keep different suppliers on separate detail lines.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
     "title": "Invoices and payment plans",
-    "body": "<p><b>Schedule payment…</b> on a detail line starts the payment journey. Choose Expected or Confirmed and enter an expected date and, when known, a confirmed payment date. Leave the recipient TBD until known, then edit the same plan to assign it. For multiple payments, select the split option and add each separately. An unsplit amount updates the forecast, not the original budget or Actuals.</p><p>When due or overdue, a payment appears at the top of Payments. Choose Paid to review the final amount and explicitly post it. The final amount may differ from the forecast; uncheck the settle option for a partial payment. A recipient is required to record paid. Attach a receipt or explicitly skip it for now. Payments are not sent automatically.</p><p>From a vendor dashboard, choose <b>Schedule payment</b> on a linked line, enter the payment amount and due date, and save. Repeat for separate dates; no automatic recurring payment is created. The simple flow splits base/fringes proportionally and cannot exceed the unscheduled balance. Use the existing advanced plan for shared payments, percentages, milestone dates or a custom split. Planning does not post to Actuals. Record paid explicitly; a shared payment is recorded once for all its allocations.</p><p><b>Add invoice…</b> records reference, type, recipient, issued/due dates, base/fringe amounts, note and supporting files. Duplicate references for the same recipient are rejected. Invoice information is entered manually; document reading is not implemented.</p><p>If an existing plan covers the same obligation, use <b>Link existing payment plan</b>. A blank invoice due date preserves a linked plan’s milestone timing. Do not enter the same bill as both an unrelated invoice and an extra plan.</p><p><b>Add payment plan…</b> creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.</p>"
+    "body": "<p><b>Schedule payment…</b> on a detail line starts the payment journey. Choose Expected or Confirmed and enter an expected date and, when known, a confirmed payment date. Leave the recipient TBD until known, then edit the same plan to assign it. For multiple payments, select the split option and add each separately. The payment amount changes the commitment forecast, not the confirmed Expected cost or Actuals. Use Confirm Expected in Details to update Expected.</p><p>When due or overdue, a payment appears at the top of Payments. Choose Paid to review the final amount and explicitly post it. The final amount may differ from the forecast; uncheck the settle option for a partial payment. A recipient is required to record paid. Attach a receipt or explicitly skip it for now. Payments are not sent automatically.</p><p>From a vendor dashboard, choose <b>Schedule payment</b> on a linked line, enter the payment amount and due date, and save. Repeat for separate dates; no automatic recurring payment is created. The simple flow splits base/fringes proportionally and cannot exceed the unscheduled balance. Use the existing advanced plan for shared payments, percentages, milestone dates or a custom split. Planning does not post to Actuals. Record paid explicitly; a shared payment is recorded once for all its allocations.</p><p><b>Add invoice…</b> records reference, type, recipient, issued/due dates, base/fringe amounts, note and supporting files. Duplicate references for the same recipient are rejected. Invoice information is entered manually; document reading is not implemented.</p><p>If an existing plan covers the same obligation, use <b>Link existing payment plan</b>. A blank invoice due date preserves a linked plan’s milestone timing. Do not enter the same bill as both an unrelated invoice and an extra plan.</p><p><b>Advanced setup</b> in Schedule payment creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
     "title": "Record paid, receipts and direct reimbursements",
-    "body": "<p>Use <b>Record paid</b> for an invoice/plan. Enter the actual amount and date; partial payments allocate across remaining shares. Select/upload a receipt or payment confirmation. To proceed without it, deliberately check <b>Skip receipt for now</b>; the payment stays flagged and cannot complete line closure until evidence is attached. Attach receipt later through payment history.</p><p><b>Record payment without invoice…</b> supports Paid directly or Reimburse someone. Store the merchant/vendor separately from the reimbursement recipient, with base/fringe amounts, real paid date and optional note. This records money already paid; it does not initiate a transfer.</p><p>Uploading or assigning a file never confirms cost or posts Actuals. Payment evidence cannot be permanently removed while a posted payment references it; archive it instead. Archived evidence remains attached.</p>"
+    "body": "<p>Use <b>Record paid</b> for an invoice/plan. Enter the actual amount and date; partial payments allocate across remaining shares. Select/upload a receipt or payment confirmation. To proceed without it, deliberately check <b>Skip receipt for now</b>; the payment stays flagged until evidence is attached. Attach receipt later through payment history.</p><p><b>Record payment without invoice…</b> supports Paid directly or Reimburse someone. Store the merchant/vendor separately from the reimbursement recipient, with base/fringe amounts, real paid date and optional note. This records money already paid; it does not initiate a transfer.</p><p>Uploading or assigning a file never confirms cost or posts Actuals. Payment evidence cannot be permanently removed while a posted payment references it; archive it instead. Archived evidence remains attached.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
@@ -67,8 +67,8 @@ window.NLBGuide = [
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
-    "title": "Expected final, Actuals, variance and closure",
-    "body": "<p><b>Budgeted</b> is your estimate. <b>Confirmed cost</b> is the agreement (or follows budget when blank). <b>Expected final</b> is the current forecast including paid amounts and remaining expected/committed cost. The budget column labels it EXPECTED FINAL; older releases called it Hot Cost or Est. Final.</p><p><b>Actuals / Net paid</b> are paid amounts minus received refunds and corrections, including preserved legacy opening values. Show Actuals reveals ACTUAL, VARIANCE and EXPECTED FINAL; Hide Actuals only hides those columns. Actuals cannot be typed directly. <b>Variance = Expected final − Budgeted</b>: red is over, green is under. Deposits alone do not create savings.</p><p><b>Finalize cost</b> sets remaining expected cost to zero when no further expense is due; it cannot bypass unpaid invoices. It is not the same as <b>Close / reopen line</b>, which checks outstanding money, expected refunds, receipts and legacy-value review. Reopen finalized cost/closed lines if circumstances change.</p>"
+    "title": "Budgeted, Expected and Actual",
+    "body": "<p><b>Budgeted</b> is the original estimate. <b>Expected</b> is the confirmed cost in Details (or follows the budget when blank), with refunds that reduce cost reflected after receipt. <b>Actual</b> is net paid, including preserved opening amounts and corrections.</p><p>The budget Expected column and its variance use Expected. The separate Expected final forecast retains higher paid or scheduled commitments and warns if they exceed Expected. This avoids hiding a known obligation. Confirming Expected never posts a payment; recording Paid never automatically edits Expected.</p><p>Previously closed or finalized lines retain their legacy state. Reopen them explicitly from the line when more payments or forecasts are needed. Paid lines may still need receipt or refund review.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ window.NLBGuide = [
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
     "title": "Contingency, locked baseline, Find and shortcuts",
-    "body": "<p>Click the Top Sheet Contingency summary to set its percentage. Budget contingency includes fringes and is included in Grand Total; cash-flow reserve remains separate from dated payments. <b>Lock Budget</b> saves Grand Total as Original Total; it does not prevent editing or freeze each line. Its baseline variance is distinct from Expected final − Budgeted. Re-lock Original replaces the baseline after confirmation; Unlock removes the comparison.</p><p>Find searches the selected budget’s account/sub-account names and detail descriptions. Cmd/Ctrl+N creates a budget; +F toggles Find; +E opens Export &amp; Share; +M opens Setup; +Z undoes supported edits; +Shift+Z redoes. Normal copy/paste works in text fields. Escape closes supported menus/dialogs or cancels confirmation.</p>"
+    "body": "<p>Click the Top Sheet Contingency summary to set its percentage. Budget contingency includes fringes and is included in Grand Total; cash-flow reserve remains separate from dated payments. <b>Lock Budget</b> saves Grand Total as Original Total; it does not prevent editing or freeze each line. Its baseline variance is distinct from Expected − Budgeted. Re-lock Original replaces the baseline after confirmation; Unlock removes the comparison.</p><p>Find searches the selected budget’s account/sub-account names and detail descriptions. Cmd/Ctrl+N creates a budget; +F toggles Find; +E opens Export &amp; Share; +M opens Setup; +Z undoes supported edits; +Shift+Z redoes. Normal copy/paste works in text fields. Escape closes supported menus/dialogs or cancels confirmation.</p>"
